{
  "_comment": "Phase 1: a single fixed encounter, but still data (pipeline \u00a73) so Phase 2's 3-5 fights is an add, not a rebuild. Grid is x:0..cols-1, y:0..rows-1; y0 is the enemies' near edge, the last row is the squad's. Two cover kinds per the pipeline's resolved assumptions: full blocks movement+LOS, partial only softens a ranged hit. `win` is the objective: {mode:'eliminate'} or {mode:'survive',rounds:N}. Elimination alone was measured unwinnable (0 wins in 300 runs) because three operators lose the damage race 2-4x to six or seven \u2014 the goal was wrong, not the numbers. Survive-N is Into the Breach's answer and it makes cover, hazards and knockback pay, because they deny damage rather than trade it. Values here were picked from turf/test/balance.mjs's 60-seed sweep, not by feel; underpass and the-yard also lost enemies because no value of N landed in the playable band at their original roster.",
